WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.963
This video shows the everyday operations of the tenant hierarchy:

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:09.316
finding and sorting the clients of a parent, fixing a setup that failed,

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:14.953
suspending and resuming several clients at once, favorites, and what the platform administrator

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:17.800
does when something changes above the parent.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.197
A firm that runs a site for each client soon has dozens of

00:00:26.197 --> 00:00:29.460
sites, and some of them need attention every day.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.691
The list of clients is where the parent's team finds a site, sees

00:00:34.691 --> 00:00:37.910
its state, and acts on one or many at a time.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.810
Above the parent, the platform administrator keeps the whole hierarchy in order:

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.960
who is a parent, who belongs to whom, and what happens when a parent disappears.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:56.361
In the parent's site, open All clients.

00:00:56.361 --> 00:01:00.425
Each row shows the name, the address and the state.

00:01:00.425 --> 00:01:03.134
The State menu narrows the list:

00:01:03.134 --> 00:01:09.763
Running, Suspended, Setting up, Setup failed, Pending removal, and Changed by platform.

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:15.172
The Sort menu orders the list by name, by newest first, or by state.

00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:19.795
Here, the State menu shows only the clients whose setup failed.

00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:29.203
A client whose site could not be created shows Setup failed, with two buttons.

00:01:29.203 --> 00:01:31.248
Retry runs the setup again.

00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:33.046
Discard gives up on it.

00:01:33.496 --> 00:01:37.904
Discard asks you to confirm, and then the address becomes free again, so

00:01:37.904 --> 00:01:40.956
you can add the client again with the same name.

00:01:45.157 --> 00:01:49.163
Tick the clients you want, and open the Actions menu.

00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:54.187
Suspend, Resume, Reload and Remove apply to every client you ticked.

00:01:54.187 --> 00:01:57.107
Remove is only for suspended clients.

00:01:57.558 --> 00:02:00.266
Here, two clients are suspended at once.

00:02:00.266 --> 00:02:05.209
Nobody can use their sites, including their own staff, until they are resumed,

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:07.328
and the State menu lists them.

00:02:17.444 --> 00:02:21.904
Tick them all and choose Resume, and both are open for business again.

00:02:26.094 --> 00:02:29.749
Open a client lists your clients with an Open link that signs you

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.191
in without a password.

00:02:31.191 --> 00:02:34.486
Click the star next to a client to make it a favorite, and

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:38.194
favorites, with the clients you opened recently, are listed first.

00:02:38.644 --> 00:02:42.959
Sign out of every client ends every session you have open in your

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:44.843
clients, on every device.

00:02:44.843 --> 00:02:49.704
Use it when you leave a shared computer, or when someone leaves your team.

00:02:53.881 --> 00:03:00.804
The platform administrator sees every parent on the Tenant Hierarchy screen, with its clients underneath.

00:03:00.804 --> 00:03:05.294
A client whose parent no longer exists is an orphan, and is listed

00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:07.851
apart, with Move and Make ordinary.

00:03:08.303 --> 00:03:15.023
Make ordinary turns the orphan into an ordinary tenant, which keeps its address and its data.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.461
On a parent's page, each client has a Move menu.

00:03:20.461 --> 00:03:23.127
Pick another parent and click Move.

00:03:23.127 --> 00:03:28.589
The client's address changes, every open session from the old parent ends, and

00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:30.800
the old parent is not asked.

00:03:31.931 --> 00:03:36.121
A parent that has no clients can be made an ordinary tenant again

00:03:36.121 --> 00:03:39.898
with Make ordinary, and it keeps its data and its address.

00:03:39.898 --> 00:03:43.911
A parent that still has clients cannot be removed by accident.

00:03:48.111 --> 00:03:52.323
Back in the parent's site, a client that the platform made an ordinary

00:03:52.323 --> 00:03:56.757
tenant, behind the parent's back, is now in the state Changed by platform,

00:03:56.757 --> 00:03:59.140
and the parent no longer controls it.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:03.131
The client the platform moved is not in this list at all any more.

00:04:03.581 --> 00:04:07.681
Click Remove from list to clear it, and the list is tidy again.

00:04:11.881 --> 00:04:16.581
Pause the sites of clients who have not paid, and resume them when they do.

00:04:17.331 --> 00:04:20.621
Find the sites that need attention with the state filter.

00:04:21.371 --> 00:04:24.751
Keep your most important clients one click away.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:29.081
Keep the hierarchy tidy after a parent changes.

00:04:31.081 --> 00:04:35.582
Filter, fix, act on several clients at once, and let the platform keep

00:04:35.582 --> 00:04:37.300
the hierarchy in order.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.801
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.341
Thanks for watching.

